# Notion-plain docs

Produce a self-contained single-file HTML page (inline `<style>`, no build step) that reads
like a clean Notion document and is ready to publish on GitHub Pages. Every page in a set
must look like it came from the same family.

Visual judgement comes from `@ruben-taste-layer.mdc`. This rule is the execution spec.

## When to use

- "Create documentation / a report / a write-up / a hub page" for a repo or project.
- Any page that will live on GitHub Pages and should look light, calm and editorial.
- Restyling an existing dark or gradient page to match this family.

## The palette (always use these exact CSS variables)

```css
:root{
  --ink:#37352F; --muted:#787774; --faint:#9B9A97;
  --line:#E9E9E7; --line-soft:#EDEDEC; --bg:#FFFFFF; --card:#FFFFFF; --tint:#F7F6F3;
  --pink:#AD1A72; --purple:#5B4FC4;
  --green:#448361; --green-bg:#EDF3EC;
  --amber:#9F6B17; --amber-bg:#FBF3DB;
  --red:#C4554D;   --red-bg:#FBE4E2;
  --gray-bg:#F1F1EF;
  --radius:6px;
}
```

## Style rules (non-negotiable)

- **White background.** No gradients, no dark sections. Even a sticky side-nav or TOC is a
  LIGHT rail (`--tint`/`--card` bg, `--muted` text) — never a dark spine.
- **System font stack:** `-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, "Apple Color Emoji", Arial, sans-serif`.
  Body 16px, line-height 1.7, `-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased`.
- **Centered content column,** `max-width: 740px` (hub/landing pages may go to ~820px for
  card grids).
- **Headings:** h1 32–36px / 700 / letter-spacing -0.01em; h2 ~23px / 700. Sections open
  with a small grey kicker or section number and a 1px `--line-soft` bottom-border divider.
- **Cards:** white, 1px `--line` border, 6px radius, no heavy shadows. Hover darkens the
  border to `--faint` (optionally fills `--tint`). No translate or lift animations.
- **Callouts:** `--tint` background, 1px `--line-soft` border, optional 3px left rule.
- **Tables:** header row `--tint` bg with `--muted` 12.5px text; cells 1px `--line-soft`
  borders; outer 1px `--line` + 6px radius + `overflow:hidden`.
- **Status / category pills:** `padding:2px 9px; border-radius:4px;` with a `*-bg`
  background and matching coloured text. Optional 7px round coloured dot via `::before`.
  Colour carries meaning: hold/ok → green, tweak/at-risk → amber, blind-spot/blocked → red,
  neutral → gray, feature/link → purple, accent → pink.
- **Links:** `--ink` with a faint underline, or `--purple` for action links.

## Page structures

**Report / write-up (max-width 740px)**

1. Topbar kicker (e.g. `MERMAID CHART · GROWTH · …`) with a small ink square logo.
2. Hero: pill row (status + method tags), H1, one-sentence `.sub`, a `.meta` row
   (method / metric / surface / author) bordered top and bottom.
3. Optional KPI strip: 4 plain stat blocks in a bordered, rounded, divided row.
4. A headline `callout`.
5. Numbered sections (`00`, `01`, …), each with a divider head, optional `.sec-sub`, then
   content: feature blocks, tables, persona grids, ranked recommendation rows.
6. Footer: caveats + sources (links).

**Hub / landing (max-width ~820px)**

- Topbar + H1 + lede.
- Sections: **Launch** (card grid), **Documentation** (feature card: 220px thumb + body),
  **Research** (same feature-card pattern, purple accent), **Latest changes** (a `LATEST`
  array of `{date,cat,title,what}` rendered by a tiny inline script; `cat` ∈
  feature/polish/infra/decision/note maps to a coloured pill).
- Footer with repo link.

## Output & workflow

1. Write a single `.html` file with everything inline.
2. For GitHub Pages: hub at `/index.html`, full doc at `/documentation/index.html`,
   reports as top-level `*.html`. Add or keep a README link to the published page.
3. Keep all sibling pages on this same palette so the set stays unified.

Starter template: `@notion-plain-template.html`
